This product is a Cangjie (仓颉) / HarmonyOS port of the EU Digital Identity
Wallet ISO/IEC 18013-5 §8 BLE proximity data-transfer library for Swift:

    eudi-lib-ios-iso18013-data-transfer
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-ios-iso18013-data-transfer

The §8 BLE framing/state machine, transfer orchestration and offline-delegate
flow are reimplemented in Cangjie with the original Swift sources used as the
reference implementation. The BLE radio layer (GATT server / client) wraps the
HarmonyOS ConnectivityKit Bluetooth GATT APIs in place of iOS CoreBluetooth
(CBPeripheralManager / CBCentralManager). NFC engagement is out of scope (the
Swift library transports over BLE only).

This product depends on and/or bundles the following third-party software:

  - eudi_lib_mdoc_security (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — session
    encryption (ECDH/HKDF/AES-GCM), reader authentication.
  - eudi_lib_mdoc_data_model (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) —
    DeviceRequest / DeviceResponse / Document / DeviceEngagement CBOR types.
  - eudi_lib_x509 (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — certificate chain
    validation (transitive, via mdoc-security).
  - eudi_lib_core_crypto (pinned third_party clone) — ECDH/AES-GCM/HKDF/digest
    primitives (transitive).
  - eudi_lib_cbor (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — CBOR encoding.
  - cangjie-stdx 1.1.3.1 (Apache-2.0) — bundled under entry/libs/stdx/.
  - OpenSSL runtime libraries (libcrypto_openssl.z.so, libssl_openssl.z.so)
    and libsecurec.so, bundled under entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ for on-device
    stdx.crypto / HUKS execution (consumed transitively via mdoc-security).

